WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.712
PostgreSQL provides several case functions UPPER
makes all

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:11.302
letters uppercase LOWER makes all letters lowercase
and is commonly

00:00:11.328 --> 00:00:16.989
useful for normalization before comparison INITCAP
capitalizes

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:22.568
words for display Be careful with names because real
capitalization

00:00:22.594 --> 00:00:28.416
can be more complex than a simple function A
cleaning rule should fit the domain

00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:32.008
rather than assuming one display convention is
universally correct
